{"query":"What were the reported daily or weekly Covid-19 death counts over time in the relevant jurisdiction(s) around and before 2020-10-21, and do they show a flat trend?","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"www.cdc.gov","snippet":"Provisional death counts by time period and jurisdiction, United States. This table has counts of deaths involving COVID-19 and other select causes of death by time-period in which the death occurred.","title":"Provisional COVID-19 Mortality Surveillance","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/nvss/vsrr/covid19/index.htm"},{"position":2,"site_name":"data.who.int","snippet":"WHO stopped requiring daily basis data reporting since August 2023 and the data presented in this dashboard are weekly frequency.","title":"COVID-19 data | WHO COVID-19 dashboard","url":"https://data.who.int/dashboards/covid19/data"},{"position":3,"site_name":"www.cdc.gov","snippet":"Counts of deaths in the most recent weeks were compared with historical trends (from 2013 to present) to determine whether the number of deaths in recent weeks was significantly higher than expected, using Farrington surveillance algorithms (1). The ‘surveillance’ package in R (2) was used to implement the Farrington algorithms, which use overdispe...","title":"Excess Deaths Associated with COVID-19 - Centers for Disease ...","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/nvss/vsrr/covid19/excess_deaths.htm"},{"position":4,"site_name":"ourworldindata.org","snippet":"This page provides data on the number of confirmed deaths from COVID-19. Research has shown that these figures are an underestimate of the total pandemic death toll. This is because of limited testing, poorly functioning death registries, challenges in determining the cause of death, and disruptions during the pandemic.","title":"Coronavirus (COVID-19) Deaths - Our World in Data","url":"https://ourworldindata.org/covid-deaths"},{"date":"Mar 31, 2023","position":5,"site_name":"data.cdc.gov","snippet":"This file contains COVID-19 death counts, death rates, and percent of total deaths by jurisdiction of residence. The data is grouped by different time periods including 3-month period, weekly, and total (cumulative since January 1, 2020).","title":"Provisional COVID-19 death counts, rates, and percent of ...","url":"https://data.cdc.gov/National-Center-for-Health-Statistics/Provisional-COVID-19-death-counts-rates-and-percen/mpx5-t7tu"},{"position":6,"site_name":"covid19dataproject.org","snippet":"On a day-to-day basis, the BroadStreet COVID-19 Data Project team of over 120 volunteers compiles and organizes data on COVID-19 case numbers and death numbers at the county level from all 50 states and the District of Columbia.","title":"Daily Numbers Release Notes & Data - covid19dataproject.org","url":"https://covid19dataproject.org/data/"},{"date":"Jul 22, 2023","position":7,"site_name":"data.who.int","snippet":"As of 25 August 2023, WHO declared that it is no longer necessary for Member States to report daily counts of cases and deaths to WHO and requested strengthening of weekly reporting. Reported data is still available attributed to specific dates (daily data) here as a download.","title":"COVID-19 deaths | WHO COVID-19 dashboard - datadot","url":"https://data.who.int/dashboards/covid19/deaths"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}